1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,750
Okay, next section, inflammatory conditions.

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:05,210
The first disorder is called acute mastitis.

3
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:06,810
Now, to understand this, let's just go back

4
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:08,210
to the whiteboard for a minute.

5
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:11,250
So here's the surface of the skin of the breast,

6
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,190
and let's pretend that this is a large duct

7
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:14,730
coming out into the nipple,

8
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:16,030
and in this particular case,

9
00:00:16,030 --> 00:00:17,870
you've got a woman who's breastfeeding.

10
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:19,030
Now, when she breastfeeds,

11
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:21,370
there's stress placed on the skin here,

12
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:23,310
and when there's stress placed on the skin,

13
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:25,970
that can result in fissures or disruption of the skin,

14
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:28,410
which then allows for entry of staph aureus.

15
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:30,170
When staph aureus comes into the breast,

16
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:33,050
it will then result in acute mastitis.

17
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:36,150
So again, acute mastitis is bacterial infection of the breast,

18
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:37,790
usually due to staph aureus,

19
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:39,830
and it's associated with breastfeeding.

20
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:41,130
Now, what's the presentation?

21
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:43,490
Well, of course, the patient's gonna have

22
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:44,690
an infection of the breast,

23
00:00:44,690 --> 00:00:47,670
and so there'll be a warm erythematous breast.

24
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:49,570
There may be a purulent nipple discharge.

25
00:00:49,570 --> 00:00:52,130
Let's say that pus begins to come out of the nipple.

26
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:55,130
That would result in a purulent nipple discharge.

27
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:56,430
Now, the treatment would be twofold.

28
00:00:56,430 --> 00:00:57,810
Number one, continued drainage.

29
00:00:57,810 --> 00:01:00,710
So, although it's awkward, if the woman was breastfeeding,

30
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:02,450
she would continue to feed the child.

31
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:04,850
And then number two, you wanna give antibiotics

32
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:06,550
to disrupt the staph aureus,

33
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:09,650
and a classic drug that would be used in this circumstance

34
00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:11,750
would be dicloxacillin.

35
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:13,330
So let's go back now and read the text.

36
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:14,290
So what do I say?

37
00:01:14,290 --> 00:01:16,470
Acute mastitis, bacterial infection of the breast,

38
00:01:16,470 --> 00:01:18,930
staph aureus, breastfeeding.

39
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:22,230
And then I say that the presentation is a warm erythematous breast

40
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:24,270
with a purulent nipple discharge.

41
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:27,130
And again, the treatment drainage and antibiotics

42
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:29,030
such as dicloxacillin.

43
00:01:29,030 --> 00:01:30,710
So those are all the high yields.

44
00:01:30,710 --> 00:01:32,670
Important to note that this particular disorder

45
00:01:32,670 --> 00:01:35,050
can progress to formation of an abscess,

46
00:01:35,050 --> 00:01:37,170
a walled-off area of inflammation.

47
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:39,250
And so that could then result in a mass.

48
00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:41,750
So in some patients with this type of presentation,

49
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:44,650
you may also feel a little bit of a mass.

50
00:01:44,650 --> 00:01:48,250
And of course, that would be due to an abscess.

51
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:50,530
The next disorder is perioductal mastitis,

52
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:53,350
and this is inflammation of the subareolar ducts.

53
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:55,030
Let's go to the whiteboard for a minute

54
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:56,090
and do a little normal,

55
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:58,390
and then this disorder becomes very straightforward.

56
00:01:58,390 --> 00:01:59,690
So here's the skin of the breast,

57
00:01:59,690 --> 00:02:02,130
and here's a large subareolar duct.

58
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:05,070
Let's remind ourselves that this large subareolar duct

59
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:09,350
is lined by epithelial cells, which are columnar.

60
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:11,110
So these are columnar epithelial cells,

61
00:02:11,110 --> 00:02:13,750
and underneath that are these myoepithelial cells,

62
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:15,450
of course, that's the normal.

63
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:17,490
Now, I want to remind you that when you look

64
00:02:17,490 --> 00:02:18,690
at the lactiferous duct,

65
00:02:18,690 --> 00:02:20,990
the ducts that are just going into the nipple,

66
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:23,830
the epithelium here of the lactiferous ducts

67
00:02:23,830 --> 00:02:26,370
is a highly specialized epithelium.

68
00:02:26,370 --> 00:02:27,770
And remember from chapter one

69
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:29,330
that highly specialized epithelia,

70
00:02:29,330 --> 00:02:32,310
they require vitamin A in order to maintain themselves,

71
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:34,110
so that this epithelium here

72
00:02:34,110 --> 00:02:36,470
is highly dependent on vitamin A.

73
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:37,750
Now, if a patient smokes,

74
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:40,270
and this disorder is predominantly seen in smokers,

75
00:02:40,270 --> 00:02:42,250
by the way, if a patient smokes,

76
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:44,790
they get a relative vitamin A deficiency,

77
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:46,990
and when they get a relative vitamin A deficiency,

78
00:02:46,990 --> 00:02:48,690
they lose the ability to maintain

79
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:50,230
this specialized epithelium,

80
00:02:50,230 --> 00:02:53,130
so that this epithelium now becomes squamous.

81
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:55,030
And as it becomes squamous,

82
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:56,690
you get this squamous metaplasia

83
00:02:56,690 --> 00:02:58,870
that occurs here in the lactiferous ducts,

84
00:02:58,870 --> 00:03:01,070
and that then would produce some degree of keratin,

85
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:02,970
which would plug these ducts.

86
00:03:02,970 --> 00:03:04,370
Now, when this duct gets plugged,

87
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:05,610
you've blocked a tube,

88
00:03:05,610 --> 00:03:07,310
and there's a general principle in pathology

89
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:08,810
that any time you block a tube,

90
00:03:08,810 --> 00:03:11,950
you're gonna get inflammation behind that block.

91
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:15,350
So now these patients get inflammation behind the duct,

92
00:03:15,350 --> 00:03:18,590
and that then is called perioductal mastitis.

93
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:20,790
Now, what are some of the consequences of this inflammation?

94
00:03:20,790 --> 00:03:21,630
Well, first of all,

95
00:03:21,630 --> 00:03:23,790
you're gonna have this big area of inflammation

96
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:26,030
with some healing and some fibrosis,

97
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:29,490
so it's gonna feel like a mass in the subareolar region,

98
00:03:29,490 --> 00:03:32,810
and so it's gonna present as a subareolar mass.

99
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:33,970
The second thing that's gonna happen

100
00:03:33,970 --> 00:03:35,310
is with all of this inflammation,

101
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:38,350
you're gonna get some fibrosis as part of the healing response,

102
00:03:38,350 --> 00:03:40,310
and that fibrosis is going to arise

103
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:41,990
through granulation tissue, of course,

104
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:43,710
and you know that granulation tissue

105
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:45,850
contains myofibroblasts,

106
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:47,690
and so myofibroblasts are gonna contract,

107
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:50,290
and they're gonna pull in the skin

108
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:51,990
right in the area of the nipple,

109
00:03:51,990 --> 00:03:53,890
and as they pull in the tissue in the skin

110
00:03:53,890 --> 00:03:54,930
by their contraction,

111
00:03:54,930 --> 00:03:56,830
they're gonna cause nipple retraction,

112
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:59,710
and so these patients can also have nipple retraction.

113
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:00,870
Now, with that as a background,

114
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:03,670
let's go back and read what I say in the book.

115
00:04:03,670 --> 00:04:06,770
So, I say that perioductal mastitis

116
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:09,270
is inflammation of the subareolar ducts,

117
00:04:09,270 --> 00:04:10,870
usually seen in smokers,

118
00:04:10,870 --> 00:04:12,210
I've already explained that,

119
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:14,850
again, because of a relative vitamin A deficiency,

120
00:04:14,850 --> 00:04:15,990
and it classically presents

121
00:04:15,990 --> 00:04:18,910
as a subareolar mass with nipple retraction.

122
00:04:18,910 --> 00:04:20,550
Now, this nipple retraction is important

123
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:23,550
because I think, from my experience with medical students,

124
00:04:23,550 --> 00:04:25,150
when they hear the word nipple retraction,

125
00:04:25,150 --> 00:04:27,590
they automatically think breast cancer.

126
00:04:27,590 --> 00:04:29,670
However, that's not always the case.

127
00:04:29,670 --> 00:04:32,790
You can have nipple retraction with, for example,

128
00:04:32,790 --> 00:04:37,230
an inflammatory condition such as perioductal mastitis.

129
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:39,730
The next disorder is called mammary duct ectasia,

130
00:04:39,730 --> 00:04:42,370
and the idea here is, again, go back to the whiteboard,

131
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:45,010
here's the skin, and then you've got this normal duct,

132
00:04:45,010 --> 00:04:47,210
and you get inflammation of the duct,

133
00:04:47,210 --> 00:04:48,870
and when you get inflammation of the duct,

134
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:51,550
you get some dilatation of that duct.

135
00:04:51,550 --> 00:04:53,810
That's called mammary duct ectasia.

136
00:04:53,810 --> 00:04:55,410
Now, as you get dilatation of the duct,

137
00:04:55,410 --> 00:04:56,910
all the inflammatory debris

138
00:04:56,910 --> 00:04:59,050
is gonna be piling up within that duct,

139
00:04:59,050 --> 00:05:00,950
and some of that inflammatory debris

140
00:05:00,950 --> 00:05:02,750
will come out of the nipple,

141
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:05,390
giving what is classically seen in this particular disorder

142
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:09,290
of a green-brown nipple discharge, very high yield.

143
00:05:09,290 --> 00:05:11,890
Green-brown nipple discharge.

144
00:05:11,890 --> 00:05:14,570
And that is basically the idea of mammary duct ectasia.

145
00:05:14,570 --> 00:05:18,210
Inflammation of the wall of the subareolar duct,

146
00:05:18,210 --> 00:05:22,210
which then results in ectasia, or dilatation, of that duct,

147
00:05:22,210 --> 00:05:24,570
and then, of course, that then is gonna result in

148
00:05:24,570 --> 00:05:28,550
this green-brown nipple discharge coming out of the duct.

149
00:05:28,550 --> 00:05:31,150
Of course, at the same time, because you've got inflammation,

150
00:05:31,150 --> 00:05:32,850
you might feel a little bit of a mass.

151
00:05:32,850 --> 00:05:35,750
So let's go now and read what I say in the book.

152
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:37,930
So I say mammary duct ectasia is inflammation

153
00:05:37,930 --> 00:05:40,330
with dilatation of the subareolar ducts.

154
00:05:40,330 --> 00:05:41,590
It's relatively rare.

155
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:45,470
It classically arises in multiparous postmenopausal women.

156
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:47,030
Now, this is very important.

157
00:05:47,030 --> 00:05:49,070
The classic history on an examination would be

158
00:05:49,070 --> 00:05:50,810
that you would have a multiparous woman,

159
00:05:50,810 --> 00:05:53,810
but I want to highlight here that this is a mass, right,

160
00:05:53,810 --> 00:05:56,370
because it's gonna form a mass because of the inflammation.

161
00:05:56,370 --> 00:05:58,970
This is a mass in a postmenopausal woman.

162
00:05:58,970 --> 00:06:00,870
Generally speaking, when we think about masses

163
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:05,050
in postmenopausal women, we're very worried about cancer.

164
00:06:05,050 --> 00:06:07,610
And that's because breast cancer is predominantly a disease

165
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:09,390
of postmenopausal women.

166
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:13,490
And so don't, so again, this is the general principle

167
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:15,450
that yes, breast cancer normally occurs

168
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:18,090
in postmenopausal women, but again, you should remember

169
00:06:18,090 --> 00:06:21,490
that not every mass in a postmenopausal woman

170
00:06:21,490 --> 00:06:22,590
is a breast cancer.

171
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:25,830
And so this is another example where examiners like to try

172
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:28,290
to make you think that they're dealing with breast cancer,

173
00:06:28,290 --> 00:06:29,690
but you're not dealing with breast cancer,

174
00:06:29,690 --> 00:06:31,770
you're dealing with mammary duct ductasia.

175
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:33,010
And what's gonna give that away

176
00:06:33,010 --> 00:06:35,110
is this green-brown nipple discharge.

177
00:06:35,110 --> 00:06:36,430
That's super high yield.

178
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:38,210
If you've got green-brown nipple discharge,

179
00:06:38,210 --> 00:06:41,310
it's highly suggestive of mammary duct ductasia.

180
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:42,550
Now, of course, if you were worried,

181
00:06:42,550 --> 00:06:45,410
and in particular because this is a postmenopausal woman,

182
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:47,650
you might be worried, so you'd do a biopsy.

183
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:49,790
And when you do a biopsy, you'll see chronic inflammation

184
00:06:49,790 --> 00:06:52,890
of the plasma cells, and the plasma cells are characteristic

185
00:06:52,890 --> 00:06:55,630
as well of this disorder.

186
00:06:55,630 --> 00:06:58,370
The last of the inflammatory disorders is fat necrosis.

187
00:06:58,370 --> 00:07:00,670
This is where you get necrosis of the breast fat.

188
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,470
Now, remember from chapter one of our texts

189
00:07:02,470 --> 00:07:05,170
that when you get fat necrosis, there's two ways.

190
00:07:05,170 --> 00:07:07,110
You can have enzymatic digestion of the fat,

191
00:07:07,110 --> 00:07:10,070
for example, as occurs with the peripancreatic fat

192
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:13,410
in pancreatitis, or you can have trauma-related disruption

193
00:07:13,410 --> 00:07:15,550
of the fat, and so in fat necrosis of the breast,

194
00:07:15,550 --> 00:07:17,550
it's usually related to trauma.

195
00:07:17,550 --> 00:07:18,650
Now, why is this important?

196
00:07:18,650 --> 00:07:20,610
Because it can present in two ways.

197
00:07:20,610 --> 00:07:23,030
It can present as a mass, so for example,

198
00:07:23,030 --> 00:07:24,550
either the woman feels the mass,

199
00:07:24,550 --> 00:07:26,330
or the physician feels the mass,

200
00:07:26,330 --> 00:07:28,790
and that's because fat necrosis was going to result

201
00:07:28,790 --> 00:07:30,990
in disruption of the fat, and some fibrosis,

202
00:07:30,990 --> 00:07:33,990
and some giant cell reaction, and some inflammation,

203
00:07:33,990 --> 00:07:35,610
which could then form a mass.

204
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:38,630
But perhaps even more classic, and particularly high yield,

205
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:42,150
is that it can also result in calcification on mammogram.

206
00:07:42,150 --> 00:07:44,210
The idea, again, is that when you have fat necrosis,

207
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:46,010
you get saponification.

208
00:07:46,010 --> 00:07:48,110
Then saponification is the addition of calcium

209
00:07:48,110 --> 00:07:50,950
to that fat necrosis, and when a woman goes for mammogram,

210
00:07:50,950 --> 00:07:52,710
they'll detect the calcifications,

211
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:54,550
and recall that calcifications are one way

212
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:56,650
by which we screen for breast cancer.

213
00:07:56,650 --> 00:07:58,550
So it could produce calcifications,

214
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:01,790
which would then require, in certain cases, a biopsy.

215
00:08:01,790 --> 00:08:03,530
And if a biopsy were to be performed,

216
00:08:03,530 --> 00:08:07,030
we would see necrotic fat with associated calcifications,

217
00:08:07,030 --> 00:08:09,610
because of the quote-unquote saponification,

218
00:08:09,610 --> 00:08:12,250
and then the presence of giant cells as well.

219
00:08:12,250 --> 00:08:14,710
And that's the classic finding in fat necrosis.

220
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:17,050
Now, I'll just remind you, especially on examinations,

221
00:08:17,050 --> 00:08:19,350
they don't usually tell you that there's a history of trauma.

222
00:08:19,350 --> 00:08:21,950
In fact, even clinically, most women will not come and say,

223
00:08:21,950 --> 00:08:23,890
oh yeah, I had this trauma.

224
00:08:23,890 --> 00:08:25,590
They don't recognize that they had trauma.

225
00:08:25,590 --> 00:08:28,270
For example, a woman plays softball

226
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:30,330
and gets hit with a softball in the chest.

227
00:08:30,330 --> 00:08:32,630
She wouldn't necessarily call that trauma,

228
00:08:32,630 --> 00:08:34,670
but that might be sufficient trauma

229
00:08:34,670 --> 00:08:36,770
to actually result in fat necrosis.

230
00:08:36,770 --> 00:08:37,810
And so when I say trauma,

231
00:08:37,810 --> 00:08:41,050
it doesn't need to be a major form of trauma.

232
00:08:41,050 --> 00:08:43,270
It could be anything that could damage the fat

233
00:08:43,270 --> 00:08:45,510
of the breast parenchyma.

234
00:08:45,510 --> 00:08:47,250
And so that closes off our section

235
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:49,590
on inflammatory disorders.

